# The wall is ordered, and what follows a failure never speaks — which under
# gavel 15 includes never being built. The left side runs and prints before
# the right side is constructed at all, so the failure in it arrives second.
#
# Under the eager wall this program printed nothing: the right operand was
# evaluated to build the description, and it died there.
pub play =
  print "a"
  >> print "{[1][5]!}"
